===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[cast]] a [[spell]] on.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To bring [[bad]] [[luck]] to.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To cause something to happen by mentioning it, usually sarcastically.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008|author=Susane Colasanti|title=When It Happens|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=knkQLyHG0UwC&pg=PT185&dq=%22jinx+it%22&hl=&cd=8&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22jinx%20it%22&f=false|chapter=46|publisher=Penguin|isbn=9781440639371
|passage=“So you'll all be near New York!” Maggie says. “We don't know for sure yet.” Sara stresses. “Don't '''jinx''' it.”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=Sally Heinrich|title=Hungry Ghosts|publisher=Hachette UK|isbn=9780734413581
|passage=I've no idea if she guessed what I was intending to do. I don't  know why I was so reluctant to talk about it, even to her. Maybe I was afraid that verbalising my intentions would '''jinx''' it in some way.}}

